  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations for NAICS 237310 are $1.6B for FY2026 to date. There were 1,570 awards, with an average award size of $1M, and obligations are up 37.0% year over year. Recent fiscal-year history shows changing yearly flows: FY21 obligations were $1.9B, FY22 were $2.1B, FY23 were $2.8B, FY24 were $2.6B, and FY25 were $1.2B. The FY26 total of $1.6B sits below the FY23 peak and above FY25. The Department of Transportation is the largest buyer so far in FY2026 to date at $565M, followed by the Department of Defense at $519M and the Department of Agriculture at $439M. Vendor concentration is visible among contractors receiving the largest obligations: KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO leads with $261M, while the next nine largest vendors range from $86.3M down to $31.7M. These figures are contract obligations and the current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date.",
